# build / editor / OS noise
#
# Nothing here may match a file the manifest lists. Compiled-artifact patterns
# are the dangerous ones: `*.o`, `*.obj` and `*.bundle` each looked like ordinary
# build noise and between them silently excluded three real language files --
# hello/full/obj, hello/full/wavefront-object and hello/full/bundle. Those files
# exist on a developer's machine and are absent from a fresh clone, so the only
# symptom was a CI failure on someone else's checkout.
#
# tests/test_gitignore_safety.py asserts that every manifest path is tracked.
*.pyc
__pycache__/
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
.idea/
.vscode/
*.bundle.tmp

# transient pipeline output (kept out of git, regenerated by scripts/)
logs/*.tmp
logs/*.log
# ...except the agent bookkeeping ledgers, which are tracked on purpose
!logs/COMMANDS.log
!logs/ERRORS.log
logs/fetch_stdout.log
logs/fetch_stderr.log
logs/gen.txt
logs/m.txt
logs/s.txt
logs/sel.txt
*.patch

# `*.bundle` was here for Ruby gems -- and it silently excluded
# hello/full/bundle/hello.bundle, a real language file that the manifest lists.
# The test suite caught it in CI: the file exists on a developer's machine and
# is simply absent from a fresh clone, so tests referencing it fail with
# FileNotFoundError and nothing local shows a problem.
#
# Ruby bundle files are ignored by an anchored path rather than a bare pattern.
# `Gemfile.lock` also matches hello/core/gemfile-lock/Gemfile.lock, which is a
# language file -- and a `!hello/...` negation cannot undo it, because the
# directory itself is matched by the earlier bare rule.
#
# This is the fourth file this class of mistake has cost, and the reason the
# .gitignore now has a test rather than a convention.
# Anchored to the repository root: a bare `Gemfile.lock` also matches
# hello/core/gemfile-lock/Gemfile.lock, which is a language file.
/[G]emfile.lock
vendor/bundle/
.bundle/

# Un-ignore the language file explicitly, so that adding a similar pattern
# above is caught by `git check-ignore` rather than by a confusing CI failure.
!hello/full/bundle/
!hello/full/**/*.bundle

# per-runner scratch (compilers, run_languages.py)
.tmp/

# run.sh artifacts (regenerated on every show)
logs/output/
logs/runners.txt
